From 3f221475081ff57397a749a9b18f366243043167 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:44:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): refuse by name a post that does not serve its
 setup's machine kind

post_serves was only the Setup pane's listing law; no posting path asked
it, so a lathe setup given a milling post (Haas, or the default Fanuc)
posted its turning ops as a milling program (G17, T M6, G43, S M3, Y
moves). A new door (posting_serves.rs) runs on every posting path -
post_setup/post_script, post_mounts/post_mounts_script and
post_per_op/post_per_op_script - before any NC text: a mount whose post
does not serve its machine's kind is refused naming the setup, its ops,
the post and the kind, and nothing is written (all or nothing per
program). Shipped posts are judged by registry name, a user's script by
its declared capabilities mask; no post serves an EDM.

Lathe test fixtures that posted turning programs through the default
Fanuc mill post now select Fanuc Lathe; the cross-drill fixture mounts a
mill-turn (a cross hole needs a live spindle).

Fixes #1232

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
